+## Connectivity, formatting, and synchronization features
+
+Kosmos-Oden's Obsidian settings group these capabilities into four panels.
+Availability depends on the host: the Obsidian plugin has the richest settings
+surface, while the standalone viewer and Tauri shell intentionally expose a
+smaller, safer subset.
+
+### Agent API (HTTP + MCP)
+
+- Read-only REST and MCP Streamable HTTP access to the sensitivity-filtered
+  Kosmos Governed Context Projection (KGCP).
+- Localhost-only binding by default, with an explicit LAN/VLAN mode and a
+  visible network-exposure warning.
+- Configurable port, fail-closed default sensitivity, independent read
+  sensitivity ceiling, required bearer authentication in LAN mode, token
+  regeneration, and deprecated query-token authentication disabled by default.
+- Graph, notes, Graphiti episodes, health, capability discovery, and traversal
+  event access where the connected runtime advertises each capability.
+- Token possession grants read transport access only; it is not identity,
+  approval, governance authority, or permission to modify notes.
+
+### Quick Connect MCP
+
+- Copyable native MCP Streamable HTTP connection material for Claude Code and
+  Claude project `.mcp.json` configuration.
+- Shared Codex app, CLI, and IDE configuration material for OpenAI clients.
+- Bundled first-party stdio configuration for Claude Desktop and other
+  stdio-only clients, without an `mcp-remote` dependency.
+- Vendor-neutral connection details and cURL health checks for other clients.
+- Generated configuration contains endpoint and authentication material and
+  must be handled as a secret; connectivity never enables write authority.
+
+### GKOS note formatting
+
+- Portable `created_at` and `updated_at` timestamps using UTC/Zulu by default
+  or local time with an explicit numeric UTC offset.
+- Canonical timestamp keys for GKX compatibility; custom keys remain ordinary
+  user frontmatter and are not silently treated as GKX fields.
+- Source-content-read-only Navigation centers and warnings for noncanonical
+  legacy center names.
+- Human-editable GKX 2.2 and 2.3 Properties, developer and custom exclusions,
+  safe repair scanning, hash-bound previews, byte-exact backups, and explicit
+  conversion controls.
+- Optional deterministic or model-assisted enrichment proposals. Suggestions
+  remain pending until reviewed and never become authoritative automatically.
+
+### Connectivity to Sync Vault
+
+- Optional Nextcloud WebDAV synchronization using an app password held by
+  Obsidian Secret Storage rather than ordinary plugin settings.
+- Configurable remote vault folder, connection test, manual synchronization,
+  startup synchronization, and scheduled synchronization.
+- Serialized execution: a second synchronization run cannot overlap an active
+  run.
+- Deletion propagation is explicit and off by default; changed-versus-deleted
+  cases remain conflicts rather than being guessed.
+- Optional `.obsidian` synchronization is separate from note synchronization
+  and carries additional plugin/configuration risk.
+- Multi-provider concurrent synchronization is not currently qualified and is
+  not advertised as available.
+
+The authoritative GKX semantics, validation, governed projections, and
+qualified filesystem effects belong to GKOS-Engine. Kosmos-Oden supplies the
+Obsidian UX, visualization, connection helpers, and host adapters. Its offline
+viewer remains read-only and does not acquire the Agent API or sync features
+merely because those controls exist in the plugin.
 
